content.text:
Now update `openOpenCodePanel` helper at bottom and add `openPermissionControls`. Current:
```ts
function openOpenCodePanel(): void {
  const panel = document.getElementById("opencode-panel");
  if (!panel) return;
  if (panel instanceof HTMLDetailsElement) panel.open = true;
  panel.scrollIntoView(...);
  panel.focus?.();
}
```
Now root is `<section tabIndex=-1>`, model details nested. Update:
```ts
function openOpenCodePanel(): void {
 const panel = document.getElementById("opencode-panel");
 if (!panel) return;
 const model = document.getElementById("opencode-model-connection");
 if (model instanceof HTMLDetailsElement) model.open = true;
 panel.scrollIntoView(...);
 panel.focus();
}
function openPermissionControls(): void {
 const permission = document.getElementById("opencode-permission");
 if (!permission) return;
 permission.scrollIntoView(...);
 const focusTarget = permission.querySelector<HTMLElement>("button, summary, h2");
 focusTarget?.focus();
}
```
Need `focus` on section with tabIndex. Good. `openPermissionControls` should also open advanced? It's separate. Permission alert is not inside details. Good.

Also `header-controls` opens model. Fine.

Edit.

